; HEX-BoomRider preset - Volatility Boom 400, $20 of headroom on a 10k demo
; Blow line: equity <= 9980 -> alert + halt (reset the demo, or deposit $20 more)
; The numbers below are the whole strategy. One 0.10-lot loss at the 0.30% stop
; costs ~$4.54 = 22.7% of the headroom, so FOUR losses fit in $20 and the 50%
; cap ($10) still admits the broker's minimum lot after the index rises ~2.2x.
; The 0.25% target against that stop pays $3.78 a win and breaks even at a 54.5%
; win rate - the first preset's 0.15/0.40 paid $2.27 for a $6.05 loss and needed
; 72.7%. Sizing takes the minimum lot while the headroom is small, then scales:
; 0.20 lots at ~$45 of headroom, 0.30 at ~$68 (20% of the headroom, floored to
; the 0.10 broker step).
InpBaselineEquity=9980.0
InpRiskPct=20.0
InpMaxRiskPct=50.0
InpTakeProfitPct=0.25
InpStopLossPct=0.30
; --- management: bank the measured target, then let the spike pay more ------
; A spike on Boom 400 is a single-tick JUMP, so an early break-even or a
; mid-target partial has nothing to act on (measured identical), and cutting a
; bleeding trade early loses 32% of the profit rate. What pays is the opposite:
; keep the 0.25% target on the base leg, and add legs while the spike is
; happening, funded only out of profit already made, all sharing one stop that
; steps up to entry+0.05% and then trails 0.30% behind the price.
; Measured, 100k ticks x 4 seeds, $20 headroom, worst calibration:
;   base only                                        $14.18/h, best trade $5
;   + this ladder (cap 30% of headroom)              $39.06/h, best trade $335
;   average loss $6.60 -> $3.20, 6 episodes at 10x a base win, 0/4 blown.
; The 30% ladder cap is what keeps one bad episode inside the 3-loss budget.
InpLockInPct=0.05
InpBackstopTPPct=1.00
InpTrailPct=0.30
InpTrailStartPct=0.40
InpMaxAdds=3
InpAddAtPct=0.20
InpAddRiskPct=100.0
InpMaxLadderLots=0.40
InpMaxLadderRiskPct=30.0
InpMaxSpreadPct=0.03
InpMagic=400400
InpHeartbeatSec=60
InpSkipLogSec=60
InpLogDir=HEX-Logs
; Pushes are sent by the CONTAINER (curl -> MT5_NOTIFY_URL), not by the EA:
; MQL5's WebRequest only accepts URLs whitelisted by hand in the terminal GUI,
; which a headless box must not depend on. Leave these two alone.
InpNotifyUrl=
InpNotifyTest=false
